WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.550
YieldShield on Monad gives your crypto
position two ways to exit.

2
00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:05.490
Keep the remaining asset,

3
00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:08.350
or exchange the position for an eligible
backing payout.

4
00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:12.050
Let's walk through how the two sides of a
pool fit together.

5
00:00:12.817 --> 00:00:14.100
Start at the faucet.

6
00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:17.250
You'll need testnet MON for network fees,

7
00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:20.150
plus the asset you want to use.

8
00:00:20.157 --> 00:00:23.850
The app supports wrapped MON and staked
MON.

9
00:00:24.497 --> 00:00:29.120
Everything shown here runs on testnet,
with valueless test assets.

10
00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:33.050
Choose Protect, pick a pool, and enter an
amount.

11
00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:37.880
Review the backing token, available
capacity, gain-sharing fees,

12
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:40.750
and waiting period before confirming in
your wallet.

13
00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:45.650
Your position then appears under
Positions, where you can manage its exits.

14
00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:47.820
Here's a simple example.

15
00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:51.430
A $100 asset has $150 of backing.

16
00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:55.980
If the asset falls 20%, taking the asset
leaves $80.

17
00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:59.430
The eligible backing exit pays $100
instead,

18
00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:02.420
and the pool receives the surrendered
asset.

19
00:01:03.317 --> 00:01:05.680
Now let the asset rise 20%.

20
00:01:05.757 --> 00:01:10.170
In this example, fees take 12% of the $20
gain.

21
00:01:10.657 --> 00:01:14.070
That leaves $117.60 in asset value.

22
00:01:14.637 --> 00:01:17.020
You can compare both exits before
choosing.

23
00:01:17.683 --> 00:01:20.950
Backing providers supply the pool's
first-loss capital.

24
00:01:21.383 --> 00:01:23.500
They earn a share of realized gains,

25
00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:25.650
and take the downside when backing is
used.

26
00:01:26.363 --> 00:01:29.703
In our falling-price example, their $150
becomes

27
00:01:29.703 --> 00:01:33.650
$130 in illustrative residual value.

28
00:01:34.317 --> 00:01:35.700
Protection has limits.

29
00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:39.750
Caps are measured in backing tokens, not
guaranteed cash.

30
00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:43.400
Waiting periods and withdrawal conditions
apply,

31
00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:46.970
and fees already realized aren't refunded
after a later loss.

32
00:01:47.917 --> 00:01:50.720
Smart-contract, pricing and token risks
remain.

33
00:01:51.557 --> 00:01:54.880
The calculator is an illustration, not a
live quote.

34
00:01:55.583 --> 00:01:56.840
Ready to explore?

35
00:01:56.900 --> 00:02:00.980
Get test tokens, compare the pools, and
try the calculator on How it works.

36
00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.200
Your asset.

37
00:02:02.263 --> 00:02:03.700
Separately supplied backing.

38
00:02:04.223 --> 00:02:05.500
Two ways to exit.

39
00:02:05.663 --> 00:02:07.720
YieldShield on Monad.
